# Environment file for the Deskmate server, consumed by both the launchd
# plist and the systemd unit in this directory. Copy this file to a path
# outside version control (the launchd plist and systemd unit both expect
# /etc/deskmate/server.env by default -- see README.md to change that),
# fill in a real admin token, and lock down its permissions:
#
#   sudo install -d -m 0755 /etc/deskmate
#   sudo install -m 0600 deskmate-server.env.example /etc/deskmate/server.env
#   sudo $EDITOR /etc/deskmate/server.env
#
# DESKMATE_ADMIN_TOKEN is the bearer secret for CLI operations and recovery.
# It cannot sign in to the web companion. Never commit a real value, and never
# put it in shell history -- generate it with something like
# `openssl rand -hex 32` and paste it directly into the file.
#
# DESKMATE_CONFIG_DIR holds per-device configs and device-identities.json. The
# identity file contains device ids and SHA-256 token digests, never bearer
# tokens, and is created 0600 with atomic replacement. Preserve this directory
# across restarts; losing the identity file requires minting and USB-provisioning
# replacement identities because the original tokens cannot be recovered.

# RUST_LOG defaults to info when unset (it defaulted to ERROR until 2026-09-23,
# which hid every device-link diagnostic and would now hide the first-run setup
# code and the sign-in links a server without SMTP prints). Set it only to
# change the level.
RUST_LOG=info

DESKMATE_SERVER_BIND=127.0.0.1:8443
DESKMATE_FIRMWARE_DIR=/var/lib/deskmate/firmware
DESKMATE_CONFIG_DIR=/var/lib/deskmate/configs
# Producer credentials live beside those, in
# DESKMATE_CONFIG_DIR/producer-credentials.json, and need no variable of their
# own: the file holds SHA-256 digests only, never a credential, so it is not a
# secret in the sense secrets.enc is. Mint one per integration with
#   curl -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer $DESKMATE_ADMIN_TOKEN" \
#     https://deskmate.example.com/v1/integrations/google/producer
# The plaintext is returned exactly once; there is no read-back route.
# Required: copy the exact firmware/version.txt value for the published image.
DESKMATE_FIRMWARE_VERSION=v2.3.0-brightness
DESKMATE_ADMIN_TOKEN=replace-with-a-real-random-token

# Required public origin. Sign-in links, cookie Origin checks, Google sign-in
# and claimed panels all use this URL. Production must use https; http is
# accepted only for localhost or a loopback IP during local development.
DESKMATE_PUBLIC_URL=https://deskmate.example.com

# Needed only for the one-time migration from the old flat config layout. The
# migration creates this instance-owner account, then keeps the old files under
# DESKMATE_CONFIG_DIR/legacy-<UTC timestamp>/.
DESKMATE_OWNER_EMAIL=you@example.com

# New-account registration is closed by default. The instance owner can change
# the stored setting later from the web companion.
DESKMATE_SIGNUPS=closed

# Optional SMTP delivery for email sign-in links. Set both values or neither;
# without them, the server prints each link in a clearly marked journal block.
# Keep SMTP credentials in this 0600 environment file.
# DESKMATE_SMTP_URL=smtps://user:password@smtp.example.com:465
# DESKMATE_MAIL_FROM=Deskmate <mail@example.com>

# DESKMATE_WEB_DIR is the built browser companion (apps/deskmate/dist), served
# at / and /assets/*. Leave it unset and those paths simply do not exist and the
# server remains API-only, which supports deployments that do not ship a UI.
#
# Deliberately a directory rather than something compiled into the binary: a UI
# change is then a `bun run build` plus a copy, with no Rust build and no
# restart. The server reads each file per request, so the new bytes are live as
# soon as they land.
#
# The path must be absolute and must contain index.html; the server refuses to
# start otherwise rather than serving 404s that look like a routing bug.
#DESKMATE_WEB_DIR=/var/lib/deskmate/web

# Google OAuth is optional. Leave every variable below commented out to run
# without integrations. To enable it, set all three required values together;
# partial or empty configuration makes the server refuse to start.
#
# Prefer the _FILE form of the client secret, for exactly the reason the secrets
# key prefers its file form: an environment value is readable through
# `systemctl show --property=Environment`, /proc/<pid>/environ, and crash dumps.
# The file must be 0600 or the server refuses to start, and naming a file that
# cannot be read is a hard failure -- it never falls back to the inline value.
# Every URL below must be https: they carry the authorization code, the client
# secret and the refresh token.
# DESKMATE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=replace-with-google-client-id
# DESKMATE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET_FILE=/etc/deskmate/google-client-secret
# DESKMATE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=replace-with-google-client-secret
# DESKMATE_GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://deskmate.example.com/v1/integrations/google/callback

# Integrations also require a 32-byte master key, base64-encoded in a separate
# owner-only (0600) file outside DESKMATE_CONFIG_DIR. The encrypted
# DESKMATE_CONFIG_DIR/secrets.enc store cannot be opened without its original
# key. Inline DESKMATE_SECRETS_KEY is supported as a less-safe fallback because
# environment values can be exposed by process/service inspection.
# DESKMATE_SECRETS_KEY_FILE=/etc/deskmate/secrets.key
# DESKMATE_SECRETS_KEY=replace-with-base64-encoded-32-byte-key

# Optional Google endpoint overrides. Normal deployments should leave these
# unset and use the built-in Google endpoints.
# DESKMATE_GOOGLE_AUTH_URI=https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/v2/auth
# DESKMATE_GOOGLE_TOKEN_URI=https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token
# DESKMATE_GOOGLE_REVOKE_URI=https://oauth2.googleapis.com/revoke

# The server-rendered faces (weather, Hacker News, RSS, token): companion/faces,
# TypeScript the server runs as a subprocess once per refresh. Unset means this
# server draws no faces -- external picture producers are unaffected. Both paths
# must be absolute, because the subprocess gets a cleared environment. Each
# account's specs live under DESKMATE_CONFIG_DIR/accounts/<account-id>/data-cards.json;
# there is no global path override.
# `deploy.sh` ships the directory and adds the first line if it is missing.
DESKMATE_FACES_DIR=/var/lib/deskmate/faces
# DESKMATE_BUN=/usr/local/bin/bun
